# Tenancy classes

Canonical guide: `docs/dev/tenancy-classes.md`.

## Rules

- Before scaffolding a new table or API, **declare its tenancy class**: **Kitchen** (org-owned), **Person** (user-global), or **Person-in-context** (user-owned + kitchen provenance).
- **Kitchen** — scope writes/reads with `organizationId` from `requireActiveGroup()` / verified membership; typically `ON DELETE CASCADE` with the org.
- **Person** — anchor on session `userId` only (e.g. nutrition goals, consent). No org tenancy.
- **Person-in-context** — owner is `userId`; `organizationId` is provenance. Writers set non-null org + name snapshots; org FK uses `ON DELETE SET NULL`. Cross-kitchen diary reads require flag `nutrition-cross-org-diary` (server-enforced).
- Never trust client-supplied `organizationId` / `userId` as the tenancy anchor.
- Do not merge Kitchen data across orgs; do not expose Person / Person-in-context nutrition to other household members.
